 "text": "Hey there, how are you? For many people, yes. A wide camera lets in more light, so it' better in daylight, and it' less likely to blow out a strong light source. That's lot of screen glare. Would you rather spend more on a laptop with a better webcam, or set up a little desk lamp beside your monitor? You can, but laptop cameras are getting better. The extra money might be worth it, especially for video calls. Then a wide camera really helps. A lamp can be your backup if the laptop camera fails.",
